            <ArticleTitle>Getting your back back to work: pain relief--where to start?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>146-52, 155-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dental health care workers are vulnerable to back and neck pain resulting from poor occupational posture. While numerous choices exist for treatment, this article will provide them with a practical approach to seeking out appropriate care for this common malady. The McKenzie treatment approach is discussed and recommendations for its application are presented to provide the reader with a starting point for treatment. For the dental health care worker experiencing pain and dysfunction of the back and/or neck, as more than half will during their careers, this article will seek to provide an overview of potential causes while creating a roadmap for seeking the most appropriate conservative &quot;antidote&quot; for their care.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
